# Product & Business Lifecycle

| Stage | Deliverable | Location | Skill |
|---|---|---|---|
| Before build | **POC validated through the internet** — hypothesis, smoke-test landing page / waitlist / interviews / small paid test, success criteria decided in advance | `docs/product/POC.md` | `mvp-poc` |
| Build | **MVP v1** — smallest version that delivers the core value to real users; scope list with explicit cuts | `docs/product/MVP.md` | `mvp-poc` |
| Build → launch | **Current business model** (Lean Canvas / Business Model Canvas, pricing, unit economics) | `docs/business/BUSINESS-MODEL.md` | `business-model` |
| After project completion | **Future business model forecast** — 3–5 year forecast with scenarios (conservative/base/optimistic), assumptions table | `docs/business/FORECAST.md` + spreadsheet | `business-model` |
| After project completion | **Investor deck** | `docs/business/INVESTOR-DECK.md` (outline) → deck | `investor-deck` |
| After project completion | **Quarterly & annual reports infrastructure** — KPI definitions, data sources, metrics tables/views, dashboard, report templates | `docs/business/reports/` + code | `periodic-reports` |

## Rules
- POC validation must be honest: fake-door tests disclose availability ("בקרוב — הצטרפו לרשימת ההמתנה"); no
  charging for things that don't exist; decide pass/fail thresholds **before** running the test.
- Every number in a business model, forecast or deck is either measured (cite the source/date) or an explicit
  assumption in the assumptions table. Never present assumptions as results.
- Forecasts and reports are management tools, not accounting or legal statements — financial statements for
  authorities are prepared with the client's accountant.
- KPIs are computed by code from the system's data (not typed by hand), so reports are reproducible.
- Keep these documents in the repo so they evolve with the product; final decks/reports are exported for sharing.
